      <activity id="4fe66866-722d-5353-a852-da8795ee7b7a" activityNameId="ad1feac6-7c76-5354-ae0c-d2bea7201135" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Azobe (SFM), standing, under bark, in rain forest</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Azobe (SFM), standing, under bark, in rain forest
data refers to wood 'under bark'. CO2 assimilation is based on 49.4% carbon in the wood including the bark (19%). Biomass energy equals gross calorific value including bark.\nTechnology: natural growth;
Synonyms: Bongassi, Ekki, Lophira alata; 
UUID: ad7548e0-2caf-31ca-908c-2d521c47bcd2
includes the CO2 absorption from air and the land use for the trees to grow (including 9% bark). Forest road area is not included in the land useDensity: 1000 kg/m3 (u=0)
Location: undefined
Technology: natural growth; relates to the forest area and CO2 from air needed to produce azobe
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ad7548e0-2caf-31ca-908c-2d521c47bcd2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
